# ez-comfy-stack multi-Spark farm profile - template.
#
# What this is: the node inventory for ./scripts/utilities/spark-farm.sh
#   (status / sync-models / dispatch). This is the multi-node profile; the
#   one-box studio profile is the repo-root example that
#   ./scripts/manage.sh setup copies. Ports, memory, image pins, download
#   throttle and the LLM knobs all belong there, never here.
# Copy and edit: cp it to config/spark-farm.env, fill in your real names, then
#   source it in the shell that runs the utility:
#     source config/spark-farm.env
#     ./scripts/utilities/spark-farm.sh status
#   With SPARK_HOSTS empty the utility fails closed and points back here
#   (scripts/utilities/spark-farm.sh:117,267).
# Never commit the real file: it names your LAN hosts and fabric addresses.
#   Commit only this example, and keep the filled copy operator-local.
# Layout: sections are the `# ---` banners and keys run most-important-first.
# Long-form docs: docs/spark-farm.mdx
# Catalog rule: MiniMax H3 is banned - see docs/licenses.md. US-safe 90s films:
#   go-see / still-here / switchyard.

# --- Management / SSH network ---------------------------------------------

# Health checks and SSH belong on the management NIC, never the 200 GbE fabric.

# SPARK_HOSTS - CSV of management-network hostnames, one per Spark; every
#   subcommand iterates it and status/sync-models/dispatch die when it is empty
#   (scripts/utilities/spark-farm.sh:44,114,265).
# Set: the names you actually SSH to (spark-N.local or DNS). Do not put fabric
#   IPs here - those go in SPARK_FABRIC_IPS.
SPARK_HOSTS=spark-0.local,spark-1.local,spark-2.local

# SPARK_USER - login for the BatchMode ssh and the rsync hops
#   (scripts/utilities/spark-farm.sh:45,90,175-176).
# Set: nvidia, the DGX Spark default and this script's own fallback. The
#   defaults differ per tool - ./scripts/utilities/setup-client.sh:129 falls
#   back to ${USER:-spark} - so set it explicitly when the account is not nvidia.
SPARK_USER=nvidia

# --- ComfyUI HTTP per node ------------------------------------------------

# One ComfyUI instance per node; the shot queue talks to these over HTTP.

# SPARK_COMFY_URLS - CSV of base URLs in the same order as SPARK_HOSTS
#   (scripts/utilities/spark-farm.sh:46,198); dispatch errors out when empty.
# Set: http://<mgmt-name>:8188 per node, same count and order as SPARK_HOSTS so
#   each worker gets the right box. Port 8188 is each node's own COMFY_PORT.
SPARK_COMFY_URLS=http://spark-0.local:8188,http://spark-1.local:8188,http://spark-2.local:8188

# --- High-bandwidth fabric ------------------------------------------------

# ConnectX-7 / RoCE addresses, used for the bulk copies only.

# SPARK_FABRIC_IPS - CSV of fabric addresses, at least two
#   (scripts/utilities/spark-farm.sh:47,163,165). sync-models rsyncs
#   ${MODELS_DIR}/comfy from entry 0 to the rest over these and refuses the
#   mgmt NIC.
# Set: the fabric-side address of each node, donor first. Confirm with a fabric
#   ping from status before a big sync.
SPARK_FABRIC_IPS=10.0.0.1,10.0.0.2,10.0.0.3

# --- Shared model cache and shot share ------------------------------------

# Same paths on every node: the farm is one shared cache, not N private ones.

# MODELS_DIR - the weights cache spark-farm.sh resolves itself
#   (scripts/utilities/spark-farm.sh:48), rsyncs over the fabric (:169) and
#   df-checks per node over SSH (:124).
# Set: identical to the one-box profile's value, and identical on every node. A
#   node with a different path is a broken farm, not a config option.
MODELS_DIR=/mnt/models

# COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR - the generated-media root the per-node shot tools read
#   (scripts/utilities/concat-shots.sh and the other utilities under
#   scripts/utilities/). spark-farm.sh itself works from FARM_SHARE below.
# Set: identical to the one-box profile's value and identical on every node, so
#   a shot printed anywhere lands in the same tree.
COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR=/mnt/comfy-output

# FARM_SHARE - directory the dispatched shots land in and that
#   concat-shots.sh reads back (scripts/utilities/spark-farm.sh:49,147,204,271).
# Set: default /mnt/comfy-output/shots is fine when COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR is shared
#   (NFS or the relay copies); move it only onto storage every node can write.
FARM_SHARE=/mnt/comfy-output/shots
